{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-09-27T08:34:43.795Z","data":{"text":"Task 4 complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented `osq inbox --follow` per the delta specs, all within scope:\n\n**`src/core/status/dispatch-follow.ts`** (new) — `followDispatch` prints the inbox text + waiting line, watches change trees via `createInvalidationHub`, polls every `inbox.pollSeconds`, and prints `<HH:MM> + ...` / `<HH:MM> - ...` deltas with a single `sound.notify()` per new batch. Single-flight derivations, tree-change hub replacement + extra derivation, throw-and-continue error handling, and clean abort. Writes nothing to the project.\n\n**`src/core/status/dispatch-text.ts`** — extracted/exported `formatDispatchItemSummary`; `itemLine` now uses it, so `osq inbox` output is byte-identical and `tests/inbox-dispatch.test.ts` passes unchanged.\n\n**`src/cli/inbox-dispatch.ts`** — added `--follow`, the seven injectable seams, `--follow --json` refusal (stderr + exit 1), and SIGINT → abort wiring.\n\n**`README.md`** — Commands entry plus a Human Attention Inbox paragraph covering what `--follow` prints, when it sounds, players tried/fallbacks, and all five `inbox` keys with defaults.\n\n**`tests/inbox-follow.test.ts`** (new) — 11 tests covering every \"Dispatch follow\" and \"Inbox follow flag\" scenario with fake watcher, manual debounce scheduler, manual poll timer, counting trees seam, and recording sound, with no real timers.\n\nVerification:\n- `node --import tsx --test tests/inbox-follow.test.ts` → 11/11 pass\n- `pnpm verify` → typechecks, build, full suite, and lint all pass\n\nResult written to `openspec/changes/098-inbox-follow-sound/.run/results/4.md`."}}
